# @@NAME@@

A [collage](https://github.com/Elagoht/collage) project, scaffolded by
`collage new -minimal`.

## Running

```
go mod tidy
cp .env.example .env.development
collage dev
```

The site is at http://localhost:3000. Templates and static files are read from
disk on every request, and the page reloads itself when one changes. A change to
Go code is rebuilt and restarted for you; one that does not compile leaves the
last good build running and says why.

`collage dev` reads `.env.development` (or `.env` when there is none). A variable
set in your shell wins over the file, and only `collage dev` reads these files.

```
go test ./...
```

## What is here

```
main.go       configuration, the static mount, and the collage CLI contract
routes.go     every page, document and action — a new route goes here
main_test.go  the tests, driving app.Handler() with no server and no port
pages/        one file per page: layout, content, route
fragments/    reusable pieces, starting with the layout
templates/    the HTML, one file per fragment
static/       CSS, JavaScript and images, at /static/
```

`collage new` without `-minimal` scaffolds a project of live demos instead — an
API action, a form, a fragment with its own URL, a JSON document — which is a
good place to see each of those working.

## Set `COLLAGE_CSRF_KEY` before deploying

It signs the tokens `{{csrfToken}}` puts in forms. Without one a key is generated
per process, and every form submitted before a restart is refused after it.

```
openssl rand -hex 32
```

## Deploying

```
collage build       # -> bin/@@NAME@@, the binary you deploy
collage export      # -> dist/, static files, for a site that needs no server
HOST=0.0.0.0 PORT=8080 COLLAGE_CSRF_KEY=... ./bin/@@NAME@@
```

Templates and static files are embedded, so the binary is the whole site.

## The collage CLI contract

`collage dev` builds this program with `go build` and runs the binary with
`COLLAGE_DEV=1` set, rebuilding and restarting it when its Go code changes;
`collage export` runs `go run . -collage-build -out <dir>`. `main.go` honours
both; if you rewrite it, keep both halves working.

A plugin's own commands are run through this program, since the `collage`
binary never loads your plugins: `go run . <command>`.
